- How would you simulate out-of-order delivery and duplicates in an automated test suite?
- What changes would you make to migrate from at-least-once to exactly-once processing in this webhook path?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests must validate complex asynchronous flows, idempotency, webhook security, and failure resilience in a distributed system.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotency keys across batch submissions
- Exactly-once processing guarantees with dedup stores
- Webhook signature validation and replay protection
- Retry/backoff strategies and dead-letter queues
- End-to-end latency and visibility across workers

## Code Example
```javascript
function verifySignature(payload, sig, secret) {
  const h = require('crypto').createHmac('sha256', secret);
  h.update(payload, 'utf8');
  const digest = h.digest('hex');
  return require('crypto').timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(digest), Buffer.from(sig));
}
```

